Package: MultiModalR
Title: Bayesian Mixture Modeling for Stratified and Hierarchical Multimodal Data
Version: 1.1.0
Date: 2026-08-29
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Gergo",
           family = "Dioszegi",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "dijogergo@gmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0003-3454-9093"))
Description: Fast Bayesian probability estimation for multimodal continuous 
    data using speed-optimized Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) implementation.
    The package provides two complementary approaches: (1) stratified mixture 
    modeling with independent fits per category (fuss_PARALLEL_mcmc), and 
    (2) a unified hierarchical mixture model with category-specific parameters 
    and shared number of components (fuss_COVARIATE_mcmc). Both approaches
    detect subpopulations, estimate mixture components, and assign observations 
    to subgroups with probability estimates.
    The methods are described in Dioszegi, G. et al. (2026) "Automatic Bayesian 
    Mixture Modeling for Multimodal Categorical Data via Integrated Mode Detection 
    and Metropolis-Hastings-within-Gibbs Sampling" (submitted).
